IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg6-s251a-agreement`
IMPORT `dg6-s251f-no-vote`
IMPORT `dg6-s251h-tender-offer`
IMPORT `dg6-s252-foreign-corporation`
IMPORT `dg6-s253-parent-subsidiary`
IMPORT `dg6-s254-joint-stock`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter IX, sections 251 to 254 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- (Source: lines 1058 to 1171 of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online made by a
-- converter script. It is not the official text.)
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law -- an
-- incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder -- asking what the Law lets them do, what it
-- requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them when corporations merge or consolidate.
-- The Secretary of State and the Court of Chancery get no seat: what section 252(d) makes the Secretary of State do appears as
-- what the corporation or the plaintiff is owed or must do.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own short lists of choices -- one for
-- each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect
-- (the agreement, the certificate, the tally of stock ...) are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and
-- the SAME layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated here. A field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed
-- placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- WHERE A LAYER-1 RULE TAKES A LIST (the classes of a subsidiary's stock, the constituent corporations of an amendment, the tallies
-- of a tender offer), the question asks about ONE item: the class with the smallest holding, your corporation and the other
-- constituent corporation, or one class (ask the question again for each class and for all the stock together).
--
-- WHERE A QUESTION'S ANSWER CAN BE "NOT COVERED" (a vote that cannot be counted, a nonstock corporation, a situation the
-- sentence does not decide), the question returns a MAYBE BOOLEAN: NOTHING is the Law's silence, not a "no".
--
-- NOTHING in this file is new law; the questions that ask for a legal conclusion the person cannot state as a fact (that an
-- agreement "complies with section 251(b)") say, in the @desc, which other question works that conclusion out.
--
-- Where the text hands a judgment to someone else it is a plain yes/no input: whether the foreign jurisdiction's law prohibits
-- the merger (section 252(a), 253(a), 254(b)), whether the board has determined that the stockholders do not recognize gain or
-- loss (section 251(g)(8)).

§ `Delaware General Corporation Law, sections 251 to 254 -- the questions of a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock`

§§ `s 251(a) and (b): merging, the board's resolution and the agreement`

-- s 251(a). Any 2 or more corporations of this State may merge into one surviving corporation, or consolidate into a new
-- resulting corporation, by an agreement that complies with, and is approved under, section 251. The two "agreement" answers are
-- legal conclusions the next questions work out from facts.
@export May our corporation merge into, or consolidate with, another corporation of this State (s 251(a))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                       IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive and absorb the others (a merger), or do they all form a new corporation (a consolidation)?
      `how many of the combining corporations are corporations of this State` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations that are combining are corporations of this State?
      `the survivor is one of the combining corporations`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger, is the corporation that survives one of the corporations that are merging? (Answer yes for a consolidation.)
      `the agreement complies with section 251`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state what section 251(b) requires and is it signed as that subsection requires? (The question about the agreement works this out from the facts.)
      `the agreement is approved in accordance with section 251`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has every corporation of this State that is a party approved the agreement as section 251 requires? (The question about approval works this out from the facts.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(a) May our corporation merge or consolidate with another corporation of this State` IF
    `s 251(a) the corporations of this State may merge or consolidate`
        `how the corporations combine`
        `how many of the combining corporations are corporations of this State`
        `the survivor is one of the combining corporations`
        `the agreement complies with section 251`
        `the agreement is approved in accordance with section 251`

-- s 251(b). "The board of directors of each corporation which desires to merge or consolidate shall adopt a resolution approving
-- an agreement of merger or consolidation and declaring its advisability."
@export Must our board adopt a resolution approving the merger agreement and declaring it advisable (s 251(b))?
GIVEN `our corporation desires to merge or consolidate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation desire to merge or consolidate with another corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(b) Must our board adopt a resolution approving the agreement and declaring its advisability` IF
    `s 251(b) the board must adopt a resolution approving an agreement and declaring its advisability` `our corporation desires to merge or consolidate`

@export Has our board adopted the resolution that section 251(b) requires of it (s 251(b))?
GIVEN `our board adopted a resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your board of directors adopted a resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation?
      `our board declared the agreement advisable`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the resolution declare the advisability of the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(b) Has our board adopted the resolution the subsection requires` IF
    `s 251(b) the board has adopted the resolution the subsection requires` `our board adopted a resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation` `our board declared the agreement advisable`

-- s 251(b)(1) to (6) and the closing paragraph: what the agreement must state, and how it is signed.
@export Does our merger agreement state everything section 251(b) requires, and is it signed as required (s 251(b))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                       IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
      `the agreement states the terms and conditions`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `the agreement states the mode of carrying it into effect`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect?
      `the agreement states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger: does the agreement state the amendments or changes to the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation, or that the certificate stays as it is? (Answer yes if not a merger.)
      `the agreement says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a consolidation: does the agreement say that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment? (Answer yes if not a consolidation.)
      `some shares are to be converted or cancelled`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some shares of a constituent corporation to be converted into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation, or cancelled?
      `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling them`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the manner of converting or cancelling those shares?
      `some shares are not to remain outstanding`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some shares of a constituent corporation not to remain outstanding?
      `their holders are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders of those shares to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity?
      `the agreement states what those holders are to receive`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state what those holders are to receive?
      `the agreement provides for cash in lieu of fractions`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities?
      `that provision is consistent with section 155`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it does: is that provision consistent with section 155 (fractions of shares)? (Answer yes if there is no such provision.)
      `the agreement was executed by an authorized person`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement executed by an authorized person?
      `the agreement is filed`                                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement (rather than a certificate in lieu of it) filed with the Secretary of State?
      `the agreement was executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is filed: was it executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103? (Answer yes if it is not filed.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(b) Does our merger agreement comply with the subsection` IF
    `s 251(b) the agreement complies with the subsection` `how the corporations combine` `my agreement`
    WHERE
        `my agreement` MEANS `s 251(b) Agreement of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS `the agreement states the terms and conditions`
            `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS `the agreement states the mode of carrying it into effect`
            `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS `the agreement states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment` IS `the agreement says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment`
            `some shares of a constituent corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or cancelled` IS `some shares are to be converted or cancelled`
            `states the manner of converting or cancelling those shares` IS `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling them`
            `some shares of a constituent corporation are not to remain outstanding` IS `some shares are not to remain outstanding`
            `the holders of those shares are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS `their holders are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity`
            `states the cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity that the holders are to receive` IS `the agreement states what those holders are to receive`
            `contains a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities` IS `the agreement provides for cash in lieu of fractions`
            `that provision is consistent with s 155` IS `that provision is consistent with section 155`
            `executed by an authorized person` IS `the agreement was executed by an authorized person`
            `is filed` IS `the agreement is filed`
            `executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS `the agreement was executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103`

-- s 251(b) closing paragraph: "Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts
-- ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the
-- agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement".
@export May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (s 251(b))?
GIVEN `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those outside facts operate upon the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(b) May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` IF
    `s 251(b) a term of the agreement may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term`

@export Is an event, or a determination or action by a person or body, a fact that a term of our merger agreement may depend on (s 251(b))?
GIVEN `what the term depends on` IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on` @desc Does the term depend on an event, on a determination or action by any person or body (including the corporation), or on something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(b) Is what the term of our merger agreement depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` IS
    `s 251(b) the item is a fact within the meaning of the closing paragraph` `what the term depends on`

§§ `s 251(c): notice of the meeting, the vote, the certificate and filing`

-- s 251(c). Notice goes "to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting": whoever holds stock is owed it.
@export Am I entitled to notice of the stockholders' meeting on the merger (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `I hold stock of the corporation, whether voting or nonvoting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold stock of the corporation, whether voting or nonvoting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Am I entitled to notice of the meeting on the merger` IF
    `s 251(c) the holder is owed notice of the meeting` `I hold stock of the corporation, whether voting or nonvoting`

-- s 251(c). Notice "at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting": counted inclusively, so notice on the 20th day before is in time.
@export By what date must notice of the meeting on the merger be given to me (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the stockholders' meeting on the merger to be held? (a date, such as 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 251(c) By what date must notice of the meeting on the merger be given` IS
    `s 251(c) the latest date on which notice of the meeting may be given` `the date of the meeting`

@export Was the notice I received of the meeting on the merger due notice (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting`                                      IS A DATE    @desc On what date is the stockholders' meeting on the merger to be held? (a date, such as 2026-03-01)
      `the date notice was given`                                    IS A DATE    @desc On what date was notice of the meeting given? (a date, such as 2026-02-05)
      `notice went to each holder of stock at the address on the corporation's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to each holder of stock, voting or nonvoting, at the holder's address as it appears on the records of the corporation?
      `the notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the time, place and purpose of the meeting?
      `the notice contains a copy of the agreement or a brief summary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a copy of the agreement or a brief summary of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Was the notice of the meeting on the merger due notice` IF
    `s 251(c) the notice of the meeting is due notice` `the notice`
    WHERE
        `the notice` MEANS `s 251(c) Notice of the meeting` WITH
            `the date of the meeting` IS `the date of the meeting`
            `the date notice was given` IS `the date notice was given`
            `notice was given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the holder's address as it appears on the records of the corporation` IS `notice went to each holder of stock at the address on the corporation's records`
            `notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting` IS `the notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting`
            `notice contains a copy of the agreement or a brief summary of it` IS `the notice contains a copy of the agreement or a brief summary`

@export Does the merger agreement have to be put to a vote of our stockholders at a meeting (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a stockholder vote unnecessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)? (The questions about those subsections work this out.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Does the merger agreement have to be put to a vote of our stockholders` IF
    `s 251(c) the agreement is to be submitted to the stockholders at a meeting` `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)`

-- s 251(c). "If a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption".
@export Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the vote section 251(c) requires (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `what kind of corporation ours is`                                IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc Is your corporation a stock corporation, or one of the three kinds of nonstock corporation?
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement`               IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favor of the agreement? (Votes, not shares, if your stock carries more or less than one vote per share.)
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`    IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock entitled to vote on the agreement carry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement` IS
    `s 251(c) the stockholders adopted the agreement` `what kind of corporation ours is` `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`

-- s 251(c) with section 102(b)(4): where the certificate of incorporation requires a larger vote than a majority.
@export Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate of incorporation requires (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `what kind of corporation ours is`                                IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc Is your corporation a stock corporation, or one of the three kinds of nonstock corporation?
      `the numerator of the fraction of the votes our certificate requires` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote does your certificate of incorporation require for this vote? Give the numerator (2 for 66 2/3%, 3 for 75%, 1 for a majority).
      `the denominator of that fraction`                                IS A NUMBER @desc The denominator of that fraction (3 for 66 2/3%, 4 for 75%, 2 for a majority).
      `the votes must exceed that fraction`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the votes exceed that fraction (as "a majority" must exceed 1/2), rather than merely reach it (as "at least 75%" need only reach it)?
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement`               IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favor of the agreement?
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`    IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock entitled to vote on the agreement carry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate requires` IS
    -- A denominator that is not above 0 is not a fraction: not covered.
    IF `the denominator of that fraction` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `s 251(c) the stockholders adopted the agreement by the vote the certificate of incorporation requires` `what kind of corporation ours is` `the vote our certificate requires` `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the vote our certificate requires` MEANS `Vote requirement` WITH
            `counted against` IS `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
            proportion IS `the numerator of the fraction of the votes our certificate requires` DIVIDED BY `the denominator of that fraction`
            `must be exceeded` IS `the votes must exceed that fraction`

-- s 251(c). The secretary or assistant secretary certifies the adoption on the agreement, unless a certificate in lieu is filed.
@export Must I, as secretary or assistant secretary, certify the stockholders' adoption on the merger agreement (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote was voted for the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote on the agreement voted for its adoption?
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of merger or consolidation being filed in lieu of filing the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify the adoption on the agreement` IF
    `s 251(c) the secretary or assistant secretary must certify the adoption on the agreement` `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote was voted for the agreement` `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of the agreement`

@export Must the merger agreement now be filed (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `each constituent corporation has adopted and certified the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each constituent corporation adopted the agreement and certified the adoption on it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Must the merger agreement now be filed` IF
    `s 251(c) the agreement is then to be filed` `each constituent corporation has adopted and certified the agreement`

-- s 251(c)(1) to (7). The certificate of merger or consolidation, which the survivor "may file" in lieu of the agreement.
@export Does our certificate of merger or consolidation state everything section 251(c) requires (s 251(c))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                 IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
      `the certificate names each constituent corporation and its state of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name and state of incorporation of each constituent corporation?
      `the certificate states that the agreement was approved, adopted, executed and acknowledged by each of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, executed and acknowledged by each constituent corporation in accordance with section 251?
      `the certificate names the surviving or resulting corporation`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name of the surviving or resulting corporation?
      `the certificate states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger: does the certificate state the amendments or changes to the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is? (Answer yes if not a merger.)
      `the certificate says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a consolidation: does the certificate state that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment? (Answer yes if not a consolidation.)
      `the certificate says the executed agreement is on file, with the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation, and give the address?
      `the certificate says a copy will be furnished on request without cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that a copy of the agreement will be furnished on request, without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation?
      `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate executed in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c) Does our certificate of merger or consolidation state what the subsection requires` IF
    `s 251(c) the certificate of merger or consolidation states what the subsection requires` `how the corporations combine` `my certificate`
    WHERE
        `my certificate` MEANS `s 251(c) Certificate of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `states the name and state of incorporation of each of the constituent corporations` IS `the certificate names each constituent corporation and its state of incorporation`
            `states that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent corporations in accordance with s 251` IS `the certificate states that the agreement was approved, adopted, executed and acknowledged by each of them`
            `states the name of the surviving or resulting corporation` IS `the certificate names the surviving or resulting corporation`
            `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS `the certificate states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment to the certificate` IS `the certificate says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment`
            `states that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation, with the address` IS `the certificate says the executed agreement is on file, with the address`
            `states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished on request and without cost to any stockholder of any constituent corporation` IS `the certificate says a copy will be furnished on request without cost`
            `executed in accordance with s 103` IS `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103`

@export Can I, as a stockholder, get a copy of the merger agreement on request without cost (s 251(c)(7))?
GIVEN `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in lieu of filing the agreement itself?
      `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of any of the corporations that merged or consolidated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(c)(7) Can I as a stockholder get a copy of the merger agreement without cost` IF
    `s 251(c)(7) the stockholder may request a copy of the agreement without cost` `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of the agreement` `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation`

-- s 251(a) read with (b), (c), (f), (g), (h): the corporation has approved the agreement "in accordance with this section".
@export Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 251 requires (s 251(a))?
GIVEN `what kind of corporation ours is`                                IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc Is your corporation a stock corporation, or one of the three kinds of nonstock corporation?
      `our board adopted the resolution section 251(b) requires`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your board adopted a resolution approving the agreement and declaring its advisability?
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement`               IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favor of the agreement? (Enter 0 if there was no vote.)
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`    IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock entitled to vote on the agreement carry?
      `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a stockholder vote unnecessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(a) Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 251 requires` IS
    `s 251(a) the constituent corporation has approved the agreement in accordance with s 251`
        `our board adopted the resolution section 251(b) requires`
        (`s 251(c) the stockholders adopted the agreement` `what kind of corporation ours is` `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`)
        `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)`

§§ `s 251(d) and (e): ending or changing the agreement before it takes effect, and the survivor's certificate`

-- s 251(d). The board of a constituent corporation may terminate the agreement, notwithstanding the stockholders' approval, if the
-- agreement so provides and it has not yet become effective.
@export May our board terminate the merger agreement after our stockholders have approved it (s 251(d))?
GIVEN `the agreement says a constituent corporation's board may terminate it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement of merger or consolidation contain a provision that the board of directors of a constituent corporation may terminate it?
      `the agreement has not yet become effective`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time not yet come at which the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) becomes effective in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(d) May our board terminate the merger agreement` IF
    `s 251(d) the board of a constituent corporation may terminate the agreement` `the agreement says a constituent corporation's board may terminate it` `the agreement has not yet become effective`

@export Must a certificate of termination of the merger or consolidation be filed (s 251(d))?
GIVEN `the agreement was terminated after it was filed`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) terminated after it was filed with the Secretary of State?
      `the agreement has not yet become effective`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the time not yet come at which the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) would have become effective in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(d) Must a certificate of termination be filed` IF
    `s 251(d) a certificate of termination must be filed` `the agreement was terminated after it was filed` `the agreement has not yet become effective`

-- s 251(d). The boards may amend the agreement if it says so and it is not yet effective; but once the stockholders of a
-- constituent corporation have adopted it, an amendment may not (1) alter what that corporation's holders receive, (2) alter the
-- survivor's certificate, or (3) alter terms to the adverse effect of a class or series of that corporation. The question is asked
-- about your corporation and one other constituent corporation.
@export May the boards amend the merger agreement after our stockholders have adopted it (s 251(d))?
GIVEN `the agreement says the boards of the constituent corporations may amend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement contain a provision that the boards of directors of the constituent corporations may amend it?
      `the agreement has not yet become effective`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time not yet come at which the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) becomes effective in accordance with section 103?
      `our stockholders had adopted the agreement before the amendment`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your corporation's stockholders adopted the agreement before the amendment was made?
      `the amendment alters what our shareholders are to receive`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment alter the amount or kind of shares, securities, cash, property or rights your corporation's holders are to receive for or on conversion of any of their shares?
      `the amendment alters terms to the adverse effect of a class or series of our stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment alter a term or condition of the agreement so as to adversely affect the holders of a class or series of your corporation's stock?
      `the other corporation's stockholders had adopted the agreement before the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the stockholders of the other constituent corporation adopted the agreement before the amendment was made?
      `the amendment alters what the other corporation's shareholders are to receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment alter the amount or kind of shares, securities, cash, property or rights the other corporation's holders are to receive?
      `the amendment alters terms to the adverse effect of a class or series of the other corporation's stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment alter a term or condition of the agreement so as to adversely affect the holders of a class or series of the other corporation's stock?
      `the amendment alters a term of the survivor's certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment alter any term of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation to be effected by the merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(d) May the boards amend the merger agreement` IF
    `s 251(d) the boards may make the amendment`
        `the agreement says the boards of the constituent corporations may amend it`
        `the agreement has not yet become effective`
        (LIST `our corporation's effect`, `the other corporation's effect`)
        `the amendment alters a term of the survivor's certificate of incorporation`
    WHERE
        `our corporation's effect` MEANS `s 251(d) Effect of an amendment on one constituent corporation` WITH
            `its stockholders adopted the agreement before the amendment` IS `our stockholders had adopted the agreement before the amendment`
            `the amendment alters the amount or kind of shares, securities, cash, property or rights to be received for or on conversion of any of its shares` IS `the amendment alters what our shareholders are to receive`
            `the amendment alters a term or condition of the agreement and adversely affects the holders of a class or series of its stock` IS `the amendment alters terms to the adverse effect of a class or series of our stock`
        `the other corporation's effect` MEANS `s 251(d) Effect of an amendment on one constituent corporation` WITH
            `its stockholders adopted the agreement before the amendment` IS `the other corporation's stockholders had adopted the agreement before the amendment`
            `the amendment alters the amount or kind of shares, securities, cash, property or rights to be received for or on conversion of any of its shares` IS `the amendment alters what the other corporation's shareholders are to receive`
            `the amendment alters a term or condition of the agreement and adversely affects the holders of a class or series of its stock` IS `the amendment alters terms to the adverse effect of a class or series of the other corporation's stock`

@export Must a certificate of amendment of the merger or consolidation be filed (s 251(d))?
GIVEN `the agreement was amended after it was filed`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement amended after it was filed with the Secretary of State?
      `the agreement has not yet become effective`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the time not yet come at which the agreement would become effective in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(d) Must a certificate of amendment be filed` IF
    `s 251(d) a certificate of amendment must be filed` `the agreement was amended after it was filed` `the agreement has not yet become effective`

-- s 251(e). In a merger the survivor's certificate of incorporation is automatically amended to the extent the agreement sets out changes.
@export Is the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation automatically amended by the merger (s 251(e))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine` IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
      `the agreement sets out changes in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement of merger set out changes in the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(e) Is the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation automatically amended` IF
    `s 251(e) the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation is automatically amended` `how the corporations combine` `the agreement sets out changes in the certificate of incorporation`

-- SITUATION: only if your merger is one that may need no stockholder vote (the surviving corporation that changes nothing, or a corporation that has issued no stock): ask "Is our merger one of these?" before showing the group.
§§ `s 251(f): a merger that needs no vote of the surviving corporation's stockholders`

-- s 251(f), first sentence. "Unless required by its certificate of incorporation, no vote of stockholders of a constituent
-- corporation surviving a merger shall be necessary to authorize a merger if (1) the agreement of merger does not amend in any
-- respect the certificate of incorporation ..., (2) each share ... is to be an identical outstanding or treasury share of the
-- surviving corporation ..., and (3) either no shares of common stock ... are to be issued or delivered ..., or [they] do not
-- exceed 20% of the shares of common stock of such constituent corporation outstanding".
@export Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we survive it and change nothing (s 251(f), first sentence)?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                   IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
      `our corporation is the corporation that survives the merger`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation the corporation that survives the merger?
      `our certificate of incorporation requires a vote of our stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation require a vote of your stockholders on this merger?
      `the agreement amends our certificate of incorporation in some respect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement of merger amend your certificate of incorporation in any respect?
      `each outstanding share of ours becomes an identical outstanding or treasury share of the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each share of your stock outstanding just before the merger to be an identical outstanding or treasury share of the surviving corporation afterwards?
      `no common stock of the survivor and nothing convertible into it is to be issued or delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are no shares of common stock of the surviving corporation, and no shares, securities or obligations convertible into such stock, to be issued or delivered under the plan of merger?
      `the number of authorized unissued or treasury common shares to be issued or delivered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many authorized unissued shares or treasury shares of common stock of the surviving corporation are to be issued or delivered under the plan of merger?
      `the number of common shares initially issuable on conversion of other securities issued under the plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of common stock are initially issuable on conversion of any other shares, securities or obligations to be issued or delivered under the plan?
      `the number of our common shares outstanding before the effective date` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of your common stock are outstanding immediately before the effective date of the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(f) Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we survive it and change nothing` IF
    `s 251(f) no vote of the stockholders is necessary under the first sentence`
        `how the corporations combine`
        `our corporation is the corporation that survives the merger`
        `our certificate of incorporation requires a vote of our stockholders`
        `the terms of the merger`
    WHERE
        `the terms of the merger` MEANS `s 251(f) Terms of the merger` WITH
            `the agreement of merger amends the certificate of incorporation of the constituent corporation in some respect` IS `the agreement amends our certificate of incorporation in some respect`
            `each outstanding share of the constituent corporation is to be an identical outstanding or treasury share of the surviving corporation` IS `each outstanding share of ours becomes an identical outstanding or treasury share of the survivor`
            `no shares of common stock of the surviving corporation, and no shares, securities or obligations convertible into such stock, are to be issued or delivered under the plan of merger` IS `no common stock of the survivor and nothing convertible into it is to be issued or delivered`
            `the number of authorized unissued or treasury shares of common stock of the surviving corporation to be issued or delivered under the plan of merger` IS `the number of authorized unissued or treasury common shares to be issued or delivered`
            `the number of shares of common stock initially issuable upon conversion of any other shares, securities or obligations to be issued or delivered under the plan` IS `the number of common shares initially issuable on conversion of other securities issued under the plan`
            `the number of shares of common stock of the constituent corporation outstanding immediately before the effective date` IS `the number of our common shares outstanding before the effective date`

-- s 251(f), second sentence. "No vote of stockholders of a constituent corporation shall be necessary to authorize a merger or
-- consolidation if no shares of the stock of such corporation shall have been issued prior to the adoption by the board".
@export Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we have issued no stock (s 251(f), second sentence)?
GIVEN `no shares of our stock had been issued before our board adopted the resolution approving the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had no shares of your corporation's stock been issued before your board adopted the resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(f) Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we have issued no stock` IF
    `s 251(f) no vote of the stockholders is necessary under the second sentence` `no shares of our stock had been issued before our board adopted the resolution approving the agreement`

@export Is a vote of our stockholders unnecessary under section 251(f), on either sentence (s 251(f))?
GIVEN `the first sentence of s 251(f) exempts the merger`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the first sentence of section 251(f) (a surviving corporation that changes nothing) exempt the merger from a stockholder vote? (The first question of this group works this out.)
      `the second sentence of s 251(f) exempts the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the second sentence of section 251(f) (no stock issued) exempt the merger from a stockholder vote? (The second question of this group works this out.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(f) Is a vote of our stockholders unnecessary under either sentence` IF
    `s 251(f) no vote of the stockholders of the constituent corporation is necessary` `the first sentence of s 251(f) exempts the merger` `the second sentence of s 251(f) exempts the merger`

-- s 251(f). The secretary or assistant secretary certifies on the agreement which sentence it was adopted under.
@export What must I, as secretary or assistant secretary, certify on an agreement adopted without a stockholder vote under section 251(f) (s 251(f))?
GIVEN `the board of the surviving corporation adopted the agreement without a vote of its stockholders under s 251(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of the surviving corporation adopt the agreement without any vote of its stockholders, pursuant to section 251(f)?
      `the sentence of s 251(f) relied on`                     IS A `s 251(f) Sentence relied on` @desc Was it adopted under the first sentence of section 251(f) (the surviving corporation that changes nothing) or the second (no stock issued)?
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of merger or consolidation being filed in lieu of filing the agreement?
GIVETH A `s 251(f) What the secretary or assistant secretary certifies`
DECIDE `s 251(f) What must the secretary or assistant secretary certify on the agreement` IS
    `s 251(f) what the secretary or assistant secretary must certify on the agreement`
        `the board of the surviving corporation adopted the agreement without a vote of its stockholders under s 251(f)`
        `the sentence of s 251(f) relied on`
        `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of the agreement`

@export By executing the agreement, do I represent that the certified facts remain true until filing (s 251(f))?
GIVEN `the agreement adopted under s 251(f) and certified is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement, adopted under section 251(f) and certified, being filed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(f) Does my executing the agreement represent that the certified facts remain true` IF
    `s 251(f) the person who executes the agreement represents that the facts stated in the certificate remain true` `the agreement adopted under s 251(f) and certified is filed`

-- SITUATION: only if your corporation is merging into its wholly-owned subsidiary to form a holding company.
§§ `s 251(g): a merger into a wholly-owned subsidiary to form a holding company`

-- Helpers that build the Entity records of paragraphs (3) and (7) from a yes/no answer. They are not law. The rules called read
-- only "a corporation or not" and "formed in this State or not": every other field is a placeholder.
GIVEN `it is formed under the laws of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`dg6 seat a corporation, formed in this State or not` `it is formed under the laws of this State` MEANS
    Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS `a corporation` (`a stock corporation`)  -- placeholder: the kind of corporation is not read
                , `where formed` IS (IF `it is formed under the laws of this State` THEN `this State` ELSE `another jurisdiction of the United States`)

-- "a corporation or limited liability company of this State": yes is a corporation of this State; no is a partnership of this State.
GIVEN `it is a corporation or limited liability company of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`dg6 seat a corporation, or a general partnership, formed in this State` `it is a corporation or limited liability company of this State` MEANS
    Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS (IF `it is a corporation or limited liability company of this State` THEN `a corporation` (`a stock corporation`) ELSE `a general partnership`)
                , `where formed` IS `this State`

-- The surviving entity: only whether it is a corporation is read; where it is formed is a placeholder.
GIVEN `it is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`dg6 seat a corporation or a limited liability company, formed in this State` `it is a corporation` MEANS
    Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS (IF `it is a corporation` THEN `a corporation` (`a stock corporation`) ELSE `a limited liability company`)
                , `where formed` IS `this State`

-- s 251(g). "Unless expressly required by its certificate of incorporation, no vote of stockholders of a constituent corporation
-- shall be necessary to authorize a merger with or into a single direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of such constituent
-- corporation if" (1) to (8). The entities of paragraphs (3) and (7) are built from yes/no answers: a placeholder says what is not read.
@export Can our corporation merge into its wholly-owned subsidiary to form a holding company without a vote of our stockholders (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `our certificate of incorporation expressly requires a vote of our stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation expressly require a vote of your stockholders on this merger?
      `we and our wholly-owned subsidiary are the only constituent entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your corporation and its direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary the only constituent entities to the merger?
      `each share of ours is converted into an equal share of the holding company with the same rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each share or fraction of a share of your capital stock converted in the merger into a share or equal fraction of a share of capital stock of a holding company having the same designations, rights, powers and preferences, and the same qualifications, limitations and restrictions?
      `the holding company is a corporation of this State`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding company a corporation of this State?
      `our corporation is a corporation of this State`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a corporation of this State?
      `the other constituent entity is a corporation or limited liability company of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsidiary that is the other constituent entity a corporation or limited liability company of this State?
      `the holding company's certificate and bylaws are identical to ours apart from the excepted provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately after the merger, do the holding company's certificate of incorporation and bylaws contain provisions identical to yours immediately before it (other than those about the incorporator, the corporate name, the registered office and agent, the initial board and initial subscribers, and completed changes of stock)?
      `we or our successor become or remain a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of the merger, does your corporation or its successor become or remain a direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company?
      `our directors become or remain the directors of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your directors become or remain the directors of the holding company when the merger takes effect?
      `the surviving entity is a corporation`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity that survives the merger a corporation (rather than, for example, a limited liability company)?
      `its organizational documents require the holding company's stockholders to approve acts that ours would have needed our stockholders to approve` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the surviving entity's organizational documents require, by specific reference to section 251(g), the approval of the holding company's stockholders (by the same vote) of any act or transaction, other than electing or removing directors or managers, that would have needed the approval of your stockholders?
      `its organizational documents also require the holding company's stockholders to approve amendments that a corporation would put in its certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the surviving entity is not a corporation: do its organizational documents also require the approval of the holding company's stockholders of any amendment that a corporation would be required to include in its certificate of incorporation? (Answer yes if it is a corporation.)
      `its organizational documents require a governing body subject to the same fiduciary duties as directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the surviving entity is not a corporation: do its organizational documents provide that its business and affairs are managed by or under the direction of a board or other governing body of individuals subject to the same fiduciary duties as directors of a corporation? (Answer yes if it is a corporation.)
      `our board has determined that our stockholders do not recognize gain or loss for federal income tax purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your board of directors determined that your stockholders do not recognize gain or loss for United States federal income tax purposes in the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g) Can our corporation merge into its wholly-owned subsidiary without a vote of our stockholders` IF
    `s 251(g) no vote of the stockholders of the constituent corporation is necessary`
        `our certificate of incorporation expressly requires a vote of our stockholders`
        `the terms of the merger`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: no rule reads which state a corporation is incorporated in other than "this State or not".
        `the terms of the merger` MEANS `s 251(g) Terms of the merger` WITH
            `the constituent corporation and its wholly-owned subsidiary are the only constituent entities to the merger` IS `we and our wholly-owned subsidiary are the only constituent entities`
            `each share or fraction of a share of the capital stock of the constituent corporation is converted in the merger into a share or equal fraction of a share of capital stock of a holding company having the same designations, rights, powers and preferences, and the same qualifications, limitations and restrictions` IS `each share of ours is converted into an equal share of the holding company with the same rights`
            `the holding company` IS (`dg6 seat a corporation, formed in this State or not` `the holding company is a corporation of this State`)
            `the constituent corporation` IS (`dg6 seat a corporation, formed in this State or not` `our corporation is a corporation of this State`)
            `the other constituent entity` IS (`dg6 seat a corporation, or a general partnership, formed in this State` `the other constituent entity is a corporation or limited liability company of this State`)
            `the certificate of incorporation and bylaws of the holding company immediately after the effective time contain provisions identical to those of the constituent corporation immediately before it, other than the excepted provisions` IS `the holding company's certificate and bylaws are identical to ours apart from the excepted provisions`
            `the constituent corporation or its successor becomes or remains a direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company` IS `we or our successor become or remain a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company`
            `the directors of the constituent corporation become or remain the directors of the holding company` IS `our directors become or remain the directors of the holding company`
            `the surviving entity` IS (`dg6 seat a corporation or a limited liability company, formed in this State` `the surviving entity is a corporation`)
            `the organizational documents of the surviving entity require the approval of the stockholders of the holding company, in addition, of acts and transactions that would have required the approval of the stockholders of the constituent corporation` IS `its organizational documents require the holding company's stockholders to approve acts that ours would have needed our stockholders to approve`
            `the organizational documents of the surviving entity require the approval of the stockholders of the holding company, in addition, of an amendment that a corporation would be required to include in its certificate of incorporation` IS `its organizational documents also require the holding company's stockholders to approve amendments that a corporation would put in its certificate`
            `the organizational documents of the surviving entity provide that its business and affairs are managed by or under the direction of a board or other governing body of individuals subject to the same fiduciary duties as directors of a corporation` IS `its organizational documents require a governing body subject to the same fiduciary duties as directors`
            `the board of directors of the constituent corporation has determined that the stockholders of the constituent corporation do not recognize gain or loss for United States federal income tax purposes` IS `our board has determined that our stockholders do not recognize gain or loss for federal income tax purposes`
-- s 251(g), closing paragraph: "holding company", as used in the subsection only.
@export Is a corporation a "holding company" for the purposes of section 251(g) (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `it is a corporation`                                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a corporation (rather than, for example, a limited liability company)?
      `from its incorporation until the merger it was at all times a wholly-owned subsidiary of the constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc From its incorporation until the merger was consummated, was it at all times a direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of the constituent corporation?
      `its capital stock is issued in the merger`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its capital stock issued in the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g) Is the corporation a holding company` IF
    `s 251(g) the entity is a holding company` (`dg6 seat a corporation or a limited liability company, formed in this State` `it is a corporation`) `from its incorporation until the merger it was at all times a wholly-owned subsidiary of the constituent corporation` `its capital stock is issued in the merger`

-- s 251(g), closing paragraph, (i): the section 203 restrictions follow the stockholders into the holding company.
@export After a holding-company merger done without our vote, do the section 203 restrictions still apply to me and my shares (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `the merger was adopted by the board without a vote of the stockholders under s 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the merger adopted by your corporation's board without any vote of its stockholders, pursuant to section 251(g)?
      `the section 203 restrictions applied to the corporation and its stockholders at the effective time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the effective time of the merger, did the restrictions of section 203 (business combinations with interested stockholders) apply to your corporation and its stockholders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g)(i) Do the section 203 restrictions still apply to the holding company and its stockholders` IS
    `s 251(g)(i) the restrictions of s 203 apply to the holding company and its stockholders` `the merger was adopted by the board without a vote of the stockholders under s 251(g)` `the section 203 restrictions applied to the corporation and its stockholders at the effective time`

@export From what date are my holding-company shares treated as acquired for the purposes of section 203 (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `the date on which I acquired my shares of the constituent corporation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you acquire the shares of the constituent corporation that were converted in the merger? (a date, such as 2019-05-17)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 251(g)(i) From what date are my holding company shares treated as acquired for section 203` IS
    `s 251(g)(i) the date on which the holding company shares are deemed acquired for s 203` `the date on which I acquired my shares of the constituent corporation`

@export Does the holding-company merger by itself make me an interested stockholder of the holding company (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `I was an interested stockholder under section 203 immediately before the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the effective time of the merger, were you an interested stockholder within the meaning of section 203?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g)(i) Does the merger by itself make me an interested stockholder of the holding company` IS
    `s 251(g)(i) the merger alone makes the stockholder an interested stockholder of the holding company` `I was an interested stockholder under section 203 immediately before the merger`

@export Do my old stock certificates now represent shares of the holding company (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `the holding company has the same corporate name as the constituent corporation had` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporate name of the holding company just after the effective time the same as the corporate name of the constituent corporation just before it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g)(ii) Do my old stock certificates represent shares of the holding company` IS
    `s 251(g)(ii) the stock certificates that represented the constituent corporation's shares represent the holding company's shares` `the holding company has the same corporate name as the constituent corporation had`

@export Do I keep my standing to bring or maintain a derivative suit after the holding-company merger (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `I had standing before the merger to sue derivatively for the constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the merger, did you have standing to institute or maintain derivative litigation on behalf of the constituent corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g)(iii) Do I keep standing to bring or maintain a derivative suit` IS
    `s 251(g)(iii) the stockholder keeps standing to institute or maintain derivative litigation` `I had standing before the merger to sue derivatively for the constituent corporation`

@export What are the organizational documents of the surviving entity for the purposes of section 251(g) (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `the surviving entity is a corporation`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving entity a corporation?
      `the surviving entity is a limited liability company`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving entity a limited liability company?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 251(g) Organizational documents`
DECIDE `s 251(g) What are the organizational documents of the surviving entity` IS
    `s 251(g) the organizational documents of the entity` `the surviving entity as an entity`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: where it is formed is not read.
        `the surviving entity as an entity` MEANS Entity WITH
            `kind of entity` IS (IF `the surviving entity is a corporation` THEN `a corporation` (`a stock corporation`) ELSE (IF `the surviving entity is a limited liability company` THEN `a limited liability company` ELSE `a general partnership`))
            `where formed` IS `this State`

@export Do the provisions section 251(g)(7) requires give the holding company's stockholders a say over electing or removing the surviving entity's directors or managers (s 251(g)(7))?
GIVEN `the provision is one that paragraph (g)(7)(A) or (B) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision one that paragraph (g)(7)(A) or (B) of section 251 requires the surviving entity's organizational documents to contain?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g)(7) Does the required provision let the holding company's stockholders approve electing or removing directors or managers` IS
    `s 251(g)(7) the provision is construed to require approval of the stockholders of the holding company to elect or remove directors or managers of the surviving entity` `the provision is one that paragraph (g)(7)(A) or (B) requires`

@export Must I, as secretary or assistant secretary, certify that the agreement was adopted under section 251(g) and that its conditions are satisfied (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `the agreement was adopted by the board without a vote of the stockholders under s 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement adopted by the board of the constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders, pursuant to section 251(g)?
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of merger or consolidation being filed in lieu of filing the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(g)` IF
    `s 251(g) the secretary or assistant secretary must certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(g) and that its conditions are satisfied` `the agreement was adopted by the board without a vote of the stockholders under s 251(g)` `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of the agreement`

@export By executing the agreement, do I represent that the certified facts remain true until filing (s 251(g))?
GIVEN `the agreement adopted under s 251(g) and certified is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement, adopted under section 251(g) and certified, being filed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(g) Does my executing the agreement represent that the certified facts remain true` IF
    `s 251(g) the person who executes the agreement represents that the facts stated in the certificate remain true` `the agreement adopted under s 251(g) and certified is filed`

-- SITUATION: only if a corporation has made, or will make, a tender offer for all your corporation's voting stock under an agreement of merger.
§§ `s 251(h): a merger after a tender offer`

-- s 251(h), lead-in. The constituent corporation "has a class or series of stock that is listed on a national securities exchange or
-- held of record by more than 2,000 holders immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger".
@export Is our corporation big enough to use the tender-offer merger: listed, or more than 2,000 holders of record (s 251(h))?
GIVEN `a class or series of our stock is listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the agreement of merger was executed, was a class or series of your corporation's stock listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of our stock` IS A NUMBER @desc Immediately before the agreement of merger was executed, what is the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of your corporation's stock?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h) Is our corporation listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` IF
    `s 251(h) the constituent corporation has stock listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` `a class or series of our stock is listed on a national securities exchange` `the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of our stock`

-- s 251(h)(3). "Immediately following the consummation of the offer ..., the stock irrevocably accepted ... and received by the depository
-- prior to expiration of such offer, together with the stock otherwise owned by the consummating corporation or its affiliates and
-- any rollover stock, equals at least such percentage of the shares of stock of such constituent corporation, and of each class or
-- series thereof, that, absent this subsection, would be required to adopt the agreement". Asked for one tally: all the stock, or one class or series.
@export Do the shares tendered, otherwise owned and rolled over reach the vote that would have been needed to adopt the merger (s 251(h)(3))?
GIVEN `the number of votes of the outstanding stock (all of it, or one class or series)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does the outstanding stock carry? (Enter all the stock, or one class or series; ask again for each class or series.)
      `the number of those votes irrevocably accepted in the offer and received by the depository before it expired` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes were irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange in the offer and received by the depository before the offer expired?
      `the number of those votes otherwise owned by the offeror or its affiliates` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes are otherwise owned by the corporation that made the offer or its affiliates?
      `the number of those votes of rollover stock`                      IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes are rollover stock?
      `the numerator of the fraction of the votes that would have been required to adopt the agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc What vote would have been required to adopt the agreement of merger, by the General Corporation Law and your certificate of incorporation, had there been a vote? Give it as a fraction of the outstanding votes: the numerator (1 for a majority, 2 for 66 2/3%, 3 for 75%).
      `the denominator of that fraction`                                 IS A NUMBER @desc The denominator of that fraction (2 for a majority, 3 for 66 2/3%, 4 for 75%).
      `the votes must exceed that fraction`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the votes exceed that fraction (as "a majority" must exceed 1/2), rather than merely reach it (as "at least 66 2/3%" need only reach it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` IS
    -- A denominator that is not above 0 is not a fraction: not covered.
    IF `the denominator of that fraction` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `s 251(h)(3) the stock held after the offer reaches the vote that would have been required for one tally` `the tally`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the tally` MEANS `s 251(h)(3) Tally of stock` WITH
            `the number of votes of the outstanding stock` IS `the number of votes of the outstanding stock (all of it, or one class or series)`
            `the number of votes of the stock irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange in the offer and received by the depository before the offer expired` IS `the number of those votes irrevocably accepted in the offer and received by the depository before it expired`
            `the number of votes of the stock otherwise owned by the consummating corporation or its affiliates` IS `the number of those votes otherwise owned by the offeror or its affiliates`
            `the number of votes of the rollover stock` IS `the number of those votes of rollover stock`
            `the vote that, absent s 251(h), would be required to adopt the agreement of merger by this chapter and by the certificate of incorporation` IS `the required vote`
        `the required vote` MEANS `Vote requirement` WITH
            `counted against` IS `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
            proportion IS `the numerator of the fraction of the votes that would have been required to adopt the agreement` DIVIDED BY `the denominator of that fraction`
            `must be exceeded` IS `the votes must exceed that fraction`

-- s 251(h): all the conditions together.
@export Can the merger go ahead without a vote of our stockholders after a tender offer (s 251(h))?
GIVEN `a class or series of our stock is listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the agreement of merger was executed, was a class or series of your corporation's stock listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of our stock` IS A NUMBER @desc Immediately before the agreement of merger was executed, what is the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of your corporation's stock?
      `our certificate of incorporation expressly requires a vote of our stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation expressly require a vote of your stockholders on this merger?
      `the agreement expressly permits or requires the merger under s 251(h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement of merger expressly permit or require the merger to be effected under section 251(h)?
      `the agreement expressly provides that the merger is effected as soon as practicable after the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement expressly provide that the merger shall be effected as soon as practicable following the consummation of the offer, if effected under section 251(h)?
      `a corporation consummated an offer for all of the outstanding stock entitled to vote, other than excluded stock, on the terms in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a corporation consummate an offer, on the terms provided in the agreement, for all of the outstanding stock of your corporation that would otherwise be entitled to vote on the agreement (other than excluded stock)?
      `the shares held after the offer reached the vote that would have been required, for all the stock and for each class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the stock accepted and received, together with the stock otherwise owned by the offeror or its affiliates and any rollover stock, reach the vote that would have been required to adopt the agreement, for all the stock and for each class or series? (The question about the shares held works this out.)
      `the corporation that made the offer merges with or into ours under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation that consummated the offer merge with or into your corporation under the agreement?
      `each other outstanding share gets the same consideration as was paid in the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each outstanding share (other than excluded stock) of each class or series that was the subject of the offer but not accepted in it to be converted in the merger into the same amount and kind of cash, property, rights or securities paid for the shares of that class or series accepted in the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h) Can the merger go ahead without a vote of our stockholders after a tender offer` IS
    `s 251(h) no vote of the stockholders of the constituent corporation is necessary`
        (`s 251(h) the constituent corporation has stock listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` `a class or series of our stock is listed on a national securities exchange` `the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of our stock`)
        `our certificate of incorporation expressly requires a vote of our stockholders`
        `the terms of the merger and the offer`
        (JUST `the shares held after the offer reached the vote that would have been required, for all the stock and for each class or series`)
    WHERE
        `the terms of the merger and the offer` MEANS `s 251(h) Terms of the merger and the offer` WITH
            `the agreement of merger expressly permits or requires the merger to be effected under s 251(h)` IS `the agreement expressly permits or requires the merger under s 251(h)`
            `the agreement of merger expressly provides that the merger shall be effected as soon as practicable following the consummation of the offer if it is effected under s 251(h)` IS `the agreement expressly provides that the merger is effected as soon as practicable after the offer`
            `a corporation has consummated an offer, on the terms provided in the agreement of merger, for all of the outstanding stock of the constituent corporation that, absent s 251(h), would be entitled to vote on the agreement, other than excluded stock` IS `a corporation consummated an offer for all of the outstanding stock entitled to vote, other than excluded stock, on the terms in the agreement`
            `the corporation that consummated the offer merges with or into the constituent corporation pursuant to the agreement of merger` IS `the corporation that made the offer merges with or into ours under the agreement`
            `each outstanding share, other than excluded stock, that is the subject of the offer and was not irrevocably accepted in it is to be converted in the merger into the same amount and kind of cash, property, rights or securities as were paid for the shares of its class or series that were irrevocably accepted` IS `each other outstanding share gets the same consideration as was paid in the offer`

-- s 251(h)(6): the terms the subsection defines, asked as a stockholder asks them.
@export Is my stock "excluded stock" that the tender offer need not be made for (s 251(h)(6)d.)?
GIVEN `who owned the stock when the offer began` IS A `s 251(h)(6)d. Owner at the commencement of the offer` @desc At the commencement of the offer, who owned the stock: the constituent corporation, the corporation making the offer, a person that owns all the offeror's stock, a wholly-owned subsidiary of any of those, or some other holder?
      `the stock is rollover stock`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the stock rollover stock (shares subject to a written agreement requiring them to be transferred, contributed or delivered to the offeror or its affiliates for stock or other equity interests in it)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h)(6)d. Is my stock excluded stock` IF
    `s 251(h)(6)d. the stock is excluded stock` `who owned the stock when the offer began` `the stock is rollover stock`

@export Is a person an affiliate of the corporation making the tender offer (s 251(h)(6)a.)?
GIVEN `the person owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person own, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the corporation making the offer?
      `the person is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the offeror`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of the corporation making the offer?
      `the person is a wholly-owned subsidiary of a person that owns all the offeror's stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of a person that owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the corporation making the offer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h)(6)a. Is the person an affiliate of the corporation making the offer` IF
    -- Placeholder: every kind of entity is a "person" (s 251(h)(6)e.), so the kind passed does not matter.
    `s 251(h)(6)a. the person is an affiliate of the corporation making the offer` `a limited liability company` `the person owns, directly or indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of the offeror` `the person is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the offeror` `the person is a wholly-owned subsidiary of a person that owns all the offeror's stock`

@export Are my tendered shares "received" for the purposes of the tender-offer count (s 251(h)(6)f.)?
GIVEN `how my shares are held`                IS A `s 251(h)(6)f. How the shares are held` @desc Are your shares certificated, uncertificated and held of record by a clearing corporation as nominee, or uncertificated and held of record by a person other than a clearing corporation as nominee?
      `the receiving step has been taken`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the step for your kind of holding been taken: physical receipt of the certificate with an executed letter of transmittal; transfer into the depository's account by an agent's message; or physical receipt of an executed letter of transmittal by the depository?
      `my certificate was canceled before the offer was consummated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your shares are certificated: was the certificate canceled before consummation of the offer? (Answer no if not.)
      `my uncertificated shares were reduced or eliminated by a sale before the offer was consummated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your shares are uncertificated: have they been reduced or eliminated by any sale before consummation of the offer? (Answer no if not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h)(6)f. Are my tendered shares received` IF
    `s 251(h)(6)f. the shares are received` `how my shares are held` `the receiving step has been taken` `my certificate was canceled before the offer was consummated` `my uncertificated shares were reduced or eliminated by a sale before the offer was consummated`

@export Are my shares "rollover stock" (s 251(h)(6)g.)?
GIVEN `my shares are subject to a written agreement to transfer them to the offeror or its affiliates for stock or equity interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares the subject of a written agreement requiring them to be transferred, contributed or delivered to the corporation making the offer or any of its affiliates in exchange for stock or other equity interests in it or an affiliate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h)(6)g. Are my shares rollover stock` IF
    `s 251(h)(6)g. the shares are rollover stock` `my shares are subject to a written agreement to transfer them to the offeror or its affiliates for stock or equity interests`

@export Are my shares still "rollover stock" when the tender-offer count is made (s 251(h)(6)g.)?
GIVEN `my shares are rollover stock`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares rollover stock (subject to a written agreement to transfer them to the offeror or its affiliates for stock or equity interests)?
      `my shares have not been transferred under the agreement just before the merger becomes effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the merger becomes effective, have your shares still not been transferred, contributed or delivered to the offeror or its affiliates under that agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h)(6)g. Are my shares still rollover stock for the tender-offer count` IF
    `s 251(h)(6)g. the shares are rollover stock for the purposes of paragraph (h)(3)` `my shares are rollover stock` `my shares have not been transferred under the agreement just before the merger becomes effective`

@export Must I, as secretary or assistant secretary, certify that the agreement was adopted under section 251(h) and that its conditions other than (h)(4) are satisfied (s 251(h))?
GIVEN `the agreement was adopted without the vote of stockholders under s 251(h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement adopted without the vote of the stockholders, pursuant to section 251(h)?
      `a certificate of merger is filed in lieu of the agreement`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of merger being filed in lieu of filing the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(h)` IF
    `s 251(h) the secretary or assistant secretary of the surviving corporation must certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(h) and that its conditions other than (h)(4) are satisfied` `the agreement was adopted without the vote of stockholders under s 251(h)` `a certificate of merger is filed in lieu of the agreement`

@export By executing the agreement, do I represent that the certified facts remain true until filing (s 251(h))?
GIVEN `the agreement adopted under s 251(h) and certified is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement, adopted under section 251(h) and certified, being filed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251(h) Does my executing the agreement represent that the certified facts remain true` IF
    `s 251(h) the person who executes the agreement represents that the facts stated in the certificate remain true` `the agreement adopted under s 251(h) and certified is filed`

-- SITUATION: only if your corporation is merging or consolidating with a corporation organized under the law of another jurisdiction. The service-of-process questions arise only if the survivor is a foreign corporation ("Has this happened to you?").
§§ `s 252: merging or consolidating with a foreign corporation`

-- s 252(a). One or more corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with one or more foreign corporations, unless the law
-- of a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits it.
@export May our corporation merge into, or consolidate with, a foreign corporation (s 252(a))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                       IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive and absorb the others (a merger), or do they all form a new corporation (a consolidation)?
      `how many of the combining corporations are corporations of this State` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations that are combining are corporations of this State?
      `how many of the combining corporations are foreign corporations`     IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations that are combining are foreign corporations (organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State)?
      `the law of a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation?
      `the survivor is one of the combining corporations`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger, is the corporation that survives one of the corporations that are merging? (Answer no for a consolidation.)
      `the resulting corporation is organized in a jurisdiction of one of the combining corporations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a consolidation, is the new resulting corporation a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of any one of the combining corporations? (Answer no for a merger.)
      `the agreement complies with section 252`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state what section 252(b) requires? (The question about the agreement works this out.)
      `the agreement is approved in accordance with section 252`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each constituent corporation adopted and approved the agreement as section 252(c) requires? (The question about approval works this out.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(a) May our corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` IF
    `s 252(a) a corporation of this State may merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation`
        `how the corporations combine`
        `how many of the combining corporations are corporations of this State`
        `how many of the combining corporations are foreign corporations`
        `the law of a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation`
        `the survivor is one of the combining corporations`
        `the resulting corporation is organized in a jurisdiction of one of the combining corporations`
        `the agreement complies with section 252`
        `the agreement is approved in accordance with section 252`

-- s 252(b). What the agreement with a foreign corporation must state.
@export Does our agreement of merger with a foreign corporation state everything section 252(b) requires (s 252(b))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                       IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
      `the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting corporation a corporation of this State?
      `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did all the constituent corporations enter into the agreement?
      `the agreement states the terms and conditions`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `the agreement states the mode of carrying it into effect`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect?
      `the agreement states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State: does the agreement state the amendments or changes to its certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the agreement says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a consolidation in which the resulting corporation is a corporation of this State: does the agreement say its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment? (Answer yes if not.)
      `some shares are to be converted or cancelled`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some shares of a constituent corporation to be converted into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation, or cancelled?
      `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling them`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the manner of converting or cancelling those shares?
      `some shares are not to remain outstanding`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some shares of a constituent corporation not to remain outstanding?
      `their holders are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders of those shares to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity?
      `the agreement states what those holders are to receive`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state what those holders are to receive?
      `the agreement provides for cash in lieu of fractions`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities?
      `that provision is consistent with section 155`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it does: is that provision consistent with section 155? (Answer yes if there is no such provision.)
      `the agreement states what the foreign jurisdictions' laws require`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement set forth the other provisions or facts that the laws of each jurisdiction under which a foreign constituent corporation is organized require? (Answer yes if they require nothing more.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(b) Does our agreement with a foreign corporation comply with the subsection` IF
    `s 252(b) the agreement complies with the subsection` `how the corporations combine` `the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State` `my agreement`
    WHERE
        `my agreement` MEANS `s 252(b) Agreement of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement` IS `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement`
            `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS `the agreement states the terms and conditions`
            `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS `the agreement states the mode of carrying it into effect`
            `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS `the agreement states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment` IS `the agreement says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment`
            `some shares of a constituent corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or cancelled` IS `some shares are to be converted or cancelled`
            `states the manner of converting or cancelling those shares` IS `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling them`
            `some shares of a constituent corporation are not to remain outstanding` IS `some shares are not to remain outstanding`
            `the holders of those shares are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS `their holders are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity`
            `states the cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity that the holders are to receive` IS `the agreement states what those holders are to receive`
            `contains a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities` IS `the agreement provides for cash in lieu of fractions`
            `that provision is consistent with s 155` IS `that provision is consistent with section 155`
            `states what the laws of each jurisdiction under which a foreign constituent corporation is organized require to be set forth` IS `the agreement states what the foreign jurisdictions' laws require`

@export May a term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depend on facts outside the agreement (s 252(b))?
GIVEN `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those outside facts operate upon the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(b) May a term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` IF
    `s 252(b) a term of the agreement may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term`

@export Is an event, or a determination or action by a person or body, a fact that a term of our agreement with a foreign corporation may depend on (s 252(b))?
GIVEN `what the term depends on` IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on` @desc Does the term depend on an event, on a determination or action by any person or body (including the corporation), or on something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(b) Is what the term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` IS
    `s 252(b) the item is a fact within the meaning of the closing paragraph` `what the term depends on`

-- s 252(c). Each constituent corporation adopts the agreement under the law it is organized under and, if a corporation of this State,
-- "in the same manner as is provided in section 251".
@export Has our corporation adopted and approved the agreement with a foreign corporation as section 252(c) requires (s 252(c))?
GIVEN `our corporation is a corporation of this State`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a corporation of this State?
      `the agreement was adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged under the law our corporation is organized under` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by your corporation in accordance with the laws under which it is organized?
      `our board adopted the resolution section 251(b) requires`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your corporation is a corporation of this State: has your board adopted a resolution approving the agreement and declaring its advisability?
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement`               IS A NUMBER @desc If your corporation is a corporation of this State: how many votes were cast in favor of the agreement? (Enter 0 if there was no vote.)
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`    IS A NUMBER @desc If your corporation is a corporation of this State: how many votes does all the outstanding stock entitled to vote on the agreement carry?
      `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your corporation is a corporation of this State: is a stockholder vote unnecessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(c) Has our corporation adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 252(c) the constituent corporation has adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires`
        `our corporation is a corporation of this State`
        `the agreement was adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged under the law our corporation is organized under`
        (`s 251(a) the constituent corporation has approved the agreement in accordance with s 251`
            `our board adopted the resolution section 251(b) requires`
            (`s 251(c) the stockholders adopted the agreement` `a stock corporation` `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`)
            `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)`)

@export When does the agreement with a foreign corporation become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State (s 252(c))?
GIVEN `the date on which a merger of corporations of this State would become effective under section 251` IS A DATE @desc On what date would a merger or consolidation of corporations of this State become effective under section 251, in accordance with section 103? (a date, such as 2027-06-30)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 252(c) When does the agreement become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` IS
    `s 252(c) the date on which the agreement becomes effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` `the date on which a merger of corporations of this State would become effective under section 251`

@export Does our certificate of merger with a foreign corporation state everything section 252(c) requires (s 252(c))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                 IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
      `the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting corporation a corporation of this State?
      `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting corporation a foreign corporation?
      `the certificate names each constituent corporation and its jurisdiction of organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name and jurisdiction of organization of each constituent corporation?
      `the certificate states that the agreement was approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the agreement has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each constituent corporation in accordance with section 252(c)?
      `the certificate names the surviving or resulting corporation`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name of the surviving or resulting corporation?
      `the certificate states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger whose survivor is a corporation of this State: does the certificate state the changes to its certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the certificate says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a consolidation whose resulting corporation is a corporation of this State: does the certificate state that its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the certificate says the executed agreement is on file, with the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation, and give the address?
      `the certificate says a copy will be furnished on request without cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that a copy of the agreement will be furnished on request, without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation?
      `the certificate states the agreement required by subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation: does the certificate state the agreement required by section 252(d) (to be served with process in this State)? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate executed in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(c) Does our certificate of merger with a foreign corporation state what the subsection requires` IF
    `s 252(c) the certificate of merger or consolidation states what the subsection requires` `how the corporations combine` `the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State` `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` `my certificate`
    WHERE
        `my certificate` MEANS `s 252(c) Certificate of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `states the name and jurisdiction of organization of each of the constituent corporations` IS `the certificate names each constituent corporation and its jurisdiction of organization`
            `states that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent corporations in accordance with s 252(c)` IS `the certificate states that the agreement was approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of them`
            `states the name of the surviving or resulting corporation` IS `the certificate names the surviving or resulting corporation`
            `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS `the certificate states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment to the certificate` IS `the certificate says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment`
            `states that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation, with the address` IS `the certificate says the executed agreement is on file, with the address`
            `states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished on request and without cost to any stockholder of any constituent corporation` IS `the certificate says a copy will be furnished on request without cost`
            `states the agreement, if any, required by subsection (d)` IS `the certificate states the agreement required by subsection (d)`
            `executed in accordance with s 103` IS `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103`

@export Can I, as a stockholder, get a copy of the agreement with a foreign corporation on request without cost (s 252(c)(7))?
GIVEN `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in lieu of filing the agreement itself?
      `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of any of the corporations that merged or consolidated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(c)(7) Can I as a stockholder get a copy of the agreement with a foreign corporation without cost` IF
    `s 252(c)(7) the stockholder may request a copy of the agreement without cost` `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of the agreement` `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation`

-- s 252(d). A foreign surviving or resulting corporation must agree to be served with process in this State.
@export Is the surviving or resulting corporation a foreign corporation that must agree to be served in this State (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `it was organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the surviving or resulting corporation organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Is the surviving or resulting corporation a foreign corporation that must agree to be served in this State` IF
    `s 252(d) the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` (`dg6 seat a corporation, formed in this State or not` (NOT `it was organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`))

@export Has the foreign surviving or resulting corporation given the agreement section 252(d) requires of it (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `it was organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the surviving or resulting corporation organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State?
      `it agrees to be served in this State for the obligations of the constituent corporations of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it agree that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding to enforce an obligation of any constituent corporation of this State?
      `it agrees to be served for obligations arising from the merger, including appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it agree that it may be served in any proceeding to enforce an obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation arising from the merger or consolidation, including a suit to enforce the right of stockholders determined in appraisal proceedings under section 262?
      `it irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings?
      `it specifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy of the process to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the address to which the Secretary of State is to mail a copy of the process?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Has the foreign surviving corporation given the agreement the subsection requires` IF
    `s 252(d) the surviving or resulting corporation has given the agreement the subsection requires`
        (`s 252(d) the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` (`dg6 seat a corporation, formed in this State or not` (NOT `it was organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`)))
        `its undertaking`
    WHERE
        `its undertaking` MEANS `s 252(d) Agreement to be served with process in this State` WITH
            `agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation of this State` IS `it agrees to be served in this State for the obligations of the constituent corporations of this State`
            `agrees that it may be served in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation arising from the merger or consolidation, including a suit to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to s 262` IS `it agrees to be served for obligations arising from the merger, including appraisal`
            `irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings` IS `it irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent`
            `specifies the address to which a copy of the process is to be mailed by the Secretary of State` IS `it specifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy of the process to`

-- s 252(d), from the plaintiff's side: a stockholder enforcing, say, an appraisal award against the foreign survivor serves the
-- Secretary of State, whom the survivor has irrevocably appointed its agent.
@export Can I serve process on the foreign surviving corporation by serving the Secretary of State (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `it was organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the surviving or resulting corporation organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State?
      `it agreed that it may be served in this State for the obligations of the constituent corporations of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it agree that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding to enforce an obligation of any constituent corporation of this State?
      `it agreed to be served for obligations arising from the merger, including appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it agree that it may be served in any proceeding to enforce an obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation arising from the merger, including a suit to enforce an appraisal award?
      `it irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State as its agent`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process?
      `it specified the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy of the process to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it specify the address to which the Secretary of State is to mail a copy of the process?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Can I serve the foreign surviving corporation through the Secretary of State` IF
        `s 252(d) the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` (`dg6 seat a corporation, formed in this State or not` (NOT `it was organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`))
    AND `s 252(d) the surviving or resulting corporation has given the agreement the subsection requires` TRUE `its undertaking`
    WHERE
        `its undertaking` MEANS `s 252(d) Agreement to be served with process in this State` WITH
            `agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation of this State` IS `it agreed that it may be served in this State for the obligations of the constituent corporations of this State`
            `agrees that it may be served in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation arising from the merger or consolidation, including a suit to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to s 262` IS `it agreed to be served for obligations arising from the merger, including appraisal`
            `irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings` IS `it irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State as its agent`
            `specifies the address to which a copy of the process is to be mailed by the Secretary of State` IS `it specified the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy of the process to`

@export May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `I serve process on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving process upon the Secretary of State by means of electronic transmission?
      `I serve it as the Secretary of State has prescribed`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving it only as the Secretary of State has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` IS
    `s 252(d) service on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission is permitted` `I serve process on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `I serve it as the Secretary of State has prescribed`

@export Have I, as plaintiff, done everything section 252(d) requires of me when serving the Secretary of State (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `I served process and any other papers in duplicate`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the process and any other papers in duplicate?
      `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under section 252(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to section 252(d)?
      `the amount I paid the Secretary of State`                          IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you pay the Secretary of State, in dollars?
      `the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)`                       IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29) for service on the Secretary of State, in dollars? (That section is not in this encoding; take the figure from it.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Have I as plaintiff done everything the subsection requires` IF
    `s 252(d) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` `I served process and any other papers in duplicate` `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under section 252(d)` `the amount I paid the Secretary of State` `the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)`

@export How much must I, as plaintiff, pay the Secretary of State when serving process under section 252(d) (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29) for service on the Secretary of State, in dollars? (That section is not in this encoding; take the figure from it.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 252(d) How much must the plaintiff pay the Secretary of State` IS
    `s 252(d) the fee the plaintiff must pay the Secretary of State` `the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)`

@export If I win, is the fee I paid the Secretary of State taxed as part of the costs (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `I prevail in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prevail in the proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Is the fee taxed as part of the costs` IF
    `s 252(d) the fee is taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding` `I prevail in the proceeding`

-- s 252(d), from the survivor's side: what it is owed when it is served through the Secretary of State.
@export Must the Secretary of State notify our corporation when process is served on the Secretary of State for us (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `process has been served upon the Secretary of State under section 252(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has process been served upon the Secretary of State in accordance with section 252(d)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Must the Secretary of State notify us of the service` IF
    `s 252(d) the Secretary of State must notify the surviving or resulting corporation of the service` `process has been served upon the Secretary of State under section 252(d)`

@export To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter notifying us of service (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `we designated a different address in writing to the Secretary of State for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for the purpose of that letter?
GIVETH A `s 252(d) Address for the Secretary of State's letter`
DECIDE `s 252(d) To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter` IS
    `s 252(d) the address to which the Secretary of State must mail the letter` `we designated a different address in writing to the Secretary of State for the purpose`

@export Is the Secretary of State's letter to us sent as section 252(d) requires (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `the letter is sent by a mail or courier service`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the letter sent by a mail or courier service?
      `the service keeps a record of mailing or deposit with the courier`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the service include a record of mailing or deposit with the courier?
      `the service keeps a record of delivery signed by the recipient`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the service include a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient?
      `the letter encloses a copy of the process and any other papers`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the letter enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Is the Secretary of State's letter sent as the subsection requires` IF
    `s 252(d) the letter is sent as the subsection requires` `the letter is sent by a mail or courier service` `the service keeps a record of mailing or deposit with the courier` `the service keeps a record of delivery signed by the recipient` `the letter encloses a copy of the process and any other papers`

@export Does the Secretary of State's record of a service on us contain everything section 252(d) requires (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `the record is kept alphabetically`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record kept alphabetically?
      `it sets forth the names of the plaintiff and the defendant`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant?
      `it sets forth the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served?
      `it sets forth that service was effected under section 252(d)`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the fact that service has been effected pursuant to section 252(d)?
      `it sets forth the return date`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the return date?
      `it sets forth the day and hour service was made`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the day and hour service was made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) Does the Secretary of State's record of the service contain what the subsection requires` IF
    `s 252(d) the Secretary of State's record of the service is what the subsection requires` `the record`
    WHERE
        `the record` MEANS `s 252(d) Record of a service of process` WITH
            `is kept alphabetically` IS `the record is kept alphabetically`
            `sets forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant` IS `it sets forth the names of the plaintiff and the defendant`
            `sets forth the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served` IS `it sets forth the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding`
            `sets forth the fact that service has been effected pursuant to s 252(d)` IS `it sets forth that service was effected under section 252(d)`
            `sets forth the return date` IS `it sets forth the return date`
            `sets forth the day and hour service was made` IS `it sets forth the day and hour service was made`

@export On a given date, must the Secretary of State still keep the record of the service made on us (s 252(d))?
GIVEN `the date on which the service of process was received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State receive the service of process? (a date, such as 2026-03-01)
      `the date I am asking about`                            IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want to know whether the record must still be kept? (a date, such as 2029-03-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(d) On the date asked about, must the Secretary of State still keep the record` IF
    `s 252(d) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record` `the date on which the service of process was received` `the date I am asking about`

-- s 252(e). Which parts of section 251 apply to a merger with a foreign corporation.
@export Does section 251(d) (terminating or amending the agreement) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation (s 252(e))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine` IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(e) Does section 251(d) apply to our merger or consolidation with a foreign corporation` IF
    `s 252(e) s 251(d) applies to the merger or consolidation` `how the corporations combine`

@export Does section 251(e) (automatic amendment of the survivor's certificate) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation (s 252(e))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine` IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
      `the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving corporation a corporation of this State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(e) Does section 251(e) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation` IF
    `s 252(e) s 251(e) applies to the merger` `how the corporations combine` `the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State`

@export Do section 251(f) and (h) (mergers needing no stockholder vote) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation (s 252(e))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine` IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one corporation survive (a merger), or is a new corporation formed (a consolidation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 252(e) Do section 251(f) and (h) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation` IF
    `s 252(e) s 251(f) and (h) apply to the merger` `how the corporations combine`

-- SITUATION: only if a corporation owns at least 90% of each class of voting stock of your corporation (or you hold stock of a parent that is merging with such a subsidiary).
§§ `s 253: a parent corporation and its subsidiary corporations`

-- s 253(a). "In any case in which (1) at least 90% of the outstanding shares of each class of the stock of a corporation or
-- corporations (other than a corporation which has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by section
-- 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)), of which class there are outstanding shares that, absent this subsection, would be entitled to vote on such
-- merger, is owned by a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation, and (2) 1 or more of such corporations is a corporation
-- of this State, unless the laws of the jurisdiction ... prohibit such merger, the parent corporation may ... merge". Asked about one
-- subsidiary and the class of its stock in which the parent's holding is smallest (if that class is at 90%, so is every other).
@export Can the parent corporation merge our corporation into itself, or itself into our corporation, by certificate of ownership and merger (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `the number of votes of the outstanding shares of the class in which the parent's holding is smallest` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the classes of your corporation's stock that have outstanding shares entitled to vote on the merger, take the class in which the parent's holding is the smallest share: how many votes do all that class's outstanding shares carry?
      `the number of those votes the parent owns`                         IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes does the parent corporation own (or does a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation own)?
      `that class has outstanding shares that would otherwise be entitled to vote on the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that class have outstanding shares that, apart from section 253, would be entitled to vote on the merger?
      `our certificate of incorporation contains the provision section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation's certificate of incorporation contain the provision that section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) requires (the holding-company provision)?
      `how many of the parent and subsidiary corporations are corporations of this State` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the parent corporation and the subsidiary corporations are corporations of this State?
      `the law of a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign corporation party to the merger is organized prohibit the merger?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a) Can the parent corporation merge us into itself or itself into us` IS
    `s 253(a) the parent corporation may merge the subsidiary corporations under this section`
        (`s 253(a)(1) the parent corporation owns at least 90% of each class of the stock of the subsidiary corporations` (LIST `our corporation as a subsidiary`))
        `how many of the parent and subsidiary corporations are corporations of this State`
        `the law of a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits the merger`
    WHERE
        `our corporation as a subsidiary` MEANS `s 253(a) Subsidiary corporation` WITH
            `its certificate of incorporation contains the provision required by s 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)` IS `our certificate of incorporation contains the provision section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) requires`
            `its classes of stock` IS LIST `the smallest-held class`
        `the smallest-held class` MEANS `s 253(a) Class of the subsidiary's stock` WITH
            `the number of votes of the outstanding shares of the class` IS `the number of votes of the outstanding shares of the class in which the parent's holding is smallest`
            `the number of those votes owned by a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation` IS `the number of those votes the parent owns`
            `there are outstanding shares of the class that, absent s 253(a), would be entitled to vote on the merger` IS `that class has outstanding shares that would otherwise be entitled to vote on the merger`

@export Does the certificate of ownership and merger state everything section 253(a) requires (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `which way the parent merges`                                        IS A `s 253(a) Direction of the merger` @desc Does the parent merge the subsidiaries into itself and assume their obligations, or does it merge itself (or itself and other subsidiaries) into one of the subsidiaries?
      `the parent corporation is a corporation of this State`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the parent corporation a corporation of this State?
      `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of ownership and merger executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103?
      `the certificate sets forth a copy of the resolution of the parent's board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate set forth a copy of the resolution of the parent corporation's board of directors to merge?
      `the certificate sets forth the date the resolution was adopted`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate set forth the date the resolution was adopted?
      `the certificate states that the parent's stockholders approved the merger after 20 days' notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the parent is a corporation of this State and does not survive: does the certificate state that a majority of the outstanding stock of the parent entitled to vote approved the merger at a meeting duly called and held after 20 days' notice? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the certificate states that the parent adopted the merger under the law it is organized under` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the parent is a foreign corporation and does not survive: does the certificate state that the parent adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the merger in accordance with the laws under which it is organized? (Answer yes if not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a) Does the certificate of ownership and merger state what the subsection requires` IF
    `s 253(a) the certificate of ownership and merger states what the subsection requires` `which way the parent merges` `the parent corporation is a corporation of this State` `the certificate`
    WHERE
        `the certificate` MEANS `s 253(a) Certificate of ownership and merger` WITH
            `executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103` IS `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103`
            `sets forth a copy of the resolution of the board of directors of the parent corporation to merge` IS `the certificate sets forth a copy of the resolution of the parent's board`
            `sets forth the date of the adoption of the resolution` IS `the certificate sets forth the date the resolution was adopted`
            `states that the proposed merger has been approved by a majority of the outstanding stock of the parent corporation entitled to vote thereon at a meeting duly called and held after 20 days' notice` IS `the certificate states that the parent's stockholders approved the merger after 20 days' notice`
            `states that the proposed merger has been adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by the parent corporation in accordance with the laws under which it is organized` IS `the certificate states that the parent adopted the merger under the law it is organized under`

@export Must the parent's board resolution tell me what I get for my shares of the subsidiary, and provide for the parent's stockholders (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `which way the parent merges`                                        IS A `s 253(a) Direction of the merger` @desc Does the parent merge the subsidiaries into itself and assume their obligations, or does it merge itself (or itself and other subsidiaries) into one of the subsidiaries?
      `the parent owns all the outstanding stock of all the subsidiaries`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent corporation own all the outstanding stock of all the subsidiary corporations that are parties to the merger?
      `the resolution states the terms, including what is to be paid for each share the parent does not own, or its cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution state the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights the surviving corporation will issue, pay, deliver or grant on surrender of each share of the subsidiary not owned by the parent, or the cancellation of some or all of such shares?
      `the resolution provides for pro rata issuance of the survivor's stock to the parent's stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the parent is not the surviving corporation: does the resolution provide for the pro rata issuance of stock of the surviving corporation to the holders of the parent's stock on surrender of any certificates? (Answer yes if the parent survives.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a) Does the parent's board resolution state what the subsection requires` IF
    `s 253(a) the resolution of the board of directors of the parent corporation states what the subsection requires` `which way the parent merges` `the parent owns all the outstanding stock of all the subsidiaries` `the resolution`
    WHERE
        `the resolution` MEANS `s 253(a) Resolution of the board of directors of the parent corporation` WITH
            `states the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted by the surviving corporation upon surrender of each share of the subsidiary corporation or corporations not owned by the parent corporation, or the cancellation of some or all of such shares` IS `the resolution states the terms, including what is to be paid for each share the parent does not own, or its cancellation`
            `includes provision for the pro rata issuance of stock of the surviving corporation to the holders of the stock of the parent corporation on surrender of any certificates therefor` IS `the resolution provides for pro rata issuance of the survivor's stock to the parent's stockholders`

@export May a term of the parent's resolution depend on facts outside the resolution (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `the resolution clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those outside facts operate upon the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a) May a term of the resolution depend on facts ascertainable outside the resolution` IF
    `s 253(a) a term of the resolution may depend on facts ascertainable outside the resolution` `the resolution clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term`

@export Is an event, or a determination or action by a person or body, a fact that a term of the parent's resolution may depend on (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `what the term depends on` IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on` @desc Does the term depend on an event, on a determination or action by any person or body (including the corporation), or on something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a) Is what the term of the resolution depends on a fact within the sentence on the resolution` IS
    `s 253(a) the item is a fact within the meaning of the sentence on the resolution` `what the term depends on`

@export Did the parent's stockholders approve the merger by the vote section 253(a) requires when the parent does not survive (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `what kind of corporation the parent is`                         IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc Is the parent a stock corporation, or one of the three kinds of nonstock corporation?
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the merger`                 IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the parent's stockholders cast in favor of the merger?
      `the number of votes of the parent's outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does all the outstanding stock of the parent entitled to vote on the merger carry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a) Did the parent's stockholders approve the merger by the required vote` IS
    `s 253(a) the stockholders of the parent corporation approved the merger` `what kind of corporation the parent is` `the number of votes cast in favor of the merger` `the number of votes of the parent's outstanding stock entitled to vote`

@export By what date must notice of the meeting of the parent's stockholders be given (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting of the parent corporation's stockholders to be held? (a date, such as 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 253(a) By what date must notice of the meeting of the parent's stockholders be given` IS
    `s 253(a) the latest date on which notice of the meeting of the parent corporation's stockholders may be given` `the date of the meeting`

@export Was the meeting of the parent's stockholders held after the notice section 253(a) requires (s 253(a))?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting`                                      IS A DATE    @desc On what date was the meeting of the parent corporation's stockholders held? (a date, such as 2026-03-01)
      `the date notice was given`                                    IS A DATE    @desc On what date was notice of the purpose of the meeting given? (a date, such as 2026-02-05)
      `the meeting was duly called and held`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the meeting duly called and held?
      `notice of the purpose went to each stockholder at the address on the records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the purpose of the meeting given to each stockholder at the stockholder's address as it appears on the records of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a) Was the meeting of the parent's stockholders held after the notice the subsection requires` IF
    `s 253(a) the meeting of the parent corporation's stockholders was held after the notice the subsection requires` `the notice`
    WHERE
        `the notice` MEANS `s 253(a) Notice of the meeting of the parent corporation's stockholders` WITH
            `the date of the meeting` IS `the date of the meeting`
            `the date notice was given` IS `the date notice was given`
            `the meeting was duly called and held` IS `the meeting was duly called and held`
            `notice of the purpose of the meeting was given to each such stockholder at the stockholder's address as it appears on the records of the corporation` IS `notice of the purpose went to each stockholder at the address on the records`

@export If the surviving corporation is foreign, which section's service-of-process rules also apply to a section 253 merger (s 253(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving corporation a foreign corporation?
      `section 258 and not section 252 is the applicable section`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is section 258 (a merger involving a nonstock corporation) rather than section 252 the section that applies to the merger of these domestic and foreign corporations?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 253(a)(1) Section that applies to a foreign surviving corporation`
DECIDE `s 253(a)(1) Which section also applies where the surviving corporation is foreign` IS
    `s 253(a)(1) the section that also applies to the merger` `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` `section 258 and not section 252 is the applicable section`

@export Must the terms of a section 253 merger obligate a foreign surviving corporation to provide the agreement and take the required actions (s 253(a)(2))?
GIVEN `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving corporation a foreign corporation?
      `the terms of the merger obligate it to provide the agreement and take the actions section 252(d) or 258(c) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving corporation to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by section 252(d) or 258(c), as applicable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(a)(2) Must the terms of the merger obligate the foreign surviving corporation` IF
    `s 253(a)(2) the terms of the merger must obligate the surviving corporation` `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` `the terms of the merger obligate it to provide the agreement and take the actions section 252(d) or 258(c) requires`

§§ `s 253(b) to (f): the name, other sections, appraisal rights, nonstock corporations, charitable status`

@export May the surviving Delaware corporation change its corporate name in a section 253 merger (s 253(b))?
GIVEN `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving corporation a Delaware corporation?
      `the parent's directors' resolution provides for the new name`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution of merger adopted by the directors of the parent corporation include a provision changing the corporate name?
      `the certificate of ownership and merger sets out that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that provision set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(b) May the surviving corporation change its corporate name` IF
    `s 253(b) the surviving corporation may change its corporate name` `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation` `the parent's directors' resolution provides for the new name` `the certificate of ownership and merger sets out that provision`

@export Has the name of the surviving corporation changed when the merger takes effect (s 253(b))?
GIVEN `the corporation may change its corporate name under section 253(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving corporation entitled to change its corporate name under section 253(b)? (The question about the name works this out.)
      `the effective date of the merger has arrived`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the effective date of the merger arrived?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(b) Has the name of the surviving corporation changed` IF
    `s 253(b) the name of the surviving corporation is changed` `the corporation may change its corporate name under section 253(b)` `the effective date of the merger has arrived`

@export Does section 251(d) (terminating or amending the agreement) apply to a section 253 merger (s 253(c))?
GIVEN `which way the parent merges` IS A `s 253(a) Direction of the merger` @desc Does the parent merge the subsidiaries into itself and assume their obligations, or does it merge itself (or itself and other subsidiaries) into one of the subsidiaries?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(c) Does section 251(d) apply to the section 253 merger` IF
    `s 253(c) s 251(d) applies to the merger` `which way the parent merges`

@export Does section 251(e) (automatic amendment of the survivor's certificate) apply to a section 253 merger (s 253(c))?
GIVEN `which way the parent merges` IS A `s 253(a) Direction of the merger` @desc Does the parent merge the subsidiaries into itself and assume their obligations, or does it merge itself (or itself and other subsidiaries) into one of the subsidiaries?
      `the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving corporation a corporation of this State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(c) Does section 251(e) apply to the section 253 merger` IF
    `s 253(c) s 251(e) applies to the merger` `which way the parent merges` `the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State`

@export In sections 251(d) and (e), what does "agreement of merger" mean when applied to a section 253 merger (s 253(c))?
GIVETH A `s 253(c) What s 251(d) and (e) call the agreement of merger`
DECIDE `s 253(c) What does agreement of merger mean in a section 253 merger` IS
    `s 253(c) the document that s 251(d) and (e) call the agreement of merger`

@export Must a merger that makes changes beyond those section 253 authorizes be done under section 251, 252, 257 or 258 (s 253(c))?
GIVEN `the merger effects changes other than those section 253 authorizes or makes applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the merger effect any changes other than those authorized by section 253 or made applicable by section 253(c)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(c) Must the merger be done under another section` IF
    `s 253(c) the merger must be accomplished under s 251, s 252, s 257 or s 258` `the merger effects changes other than those section 253 authorizes or makes applicable`

@export Does section 262 (appraisal) apply to a section 253 merger (s 253(c))?
GIVEN `the subsidiary is a Delaware corporation party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsidiary a corporation of this State that is a party to the merger?
      `the parent owns all the stock of the subsidiary just before the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent corporation own all of the stock of the subsidiary immediately before the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(c) Does section 262 apply to the section 253 merger` IF
    `s 253(c) s 262 applies to the merger` `the subsidiary is a Delaware corporation party to the merger` `the parent owns all the stock of the subsidiary just before the merger`

@export Do I have appraisal rights as a stockholder of the subsidiary in a section 253 merger (s 253(d))?
GIVEN `the subsidiary is a Delaware corporation party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation whose stock you hold a corporation of this State that is a party to the merger?
      `the parent owns all the stock of the subsidiary just before the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent corporation own all of the stock of the subsidiary immediately before the merger? (If you hold any of it, it does not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(d) Do I have appraisal rights as a stockholder of the subsidiary` IF
    `s 253(d) the stockholders of the subsidiary have appraisal rights as set forth in s 262` `the subsidiary is a Delaware corporation party to the merger` `the parent owns all the stock of the subsidiary just before the merger`

@export Does section 253 apply where our parent is a nonstock corporation (s 253(e))?
GIVEN `what kind of corporation the parent is`                        IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc Is the parent a stock corporation, or one of the three kinds of nonstock corporation?
      `the parent is the surviving corporation of the merger`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the parent the corporation that survives the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(e) Does section 253 apply to our nonstock parent` IF
    `s 253(e) this section applies to the nonstock corporation` `what kind of corporation the parent is` `the parent is the surviving corporation of the merger`

@export In a section 253 merger with a nonstock parent, are references to the parent's directors and board read as its governing body (s 253(e))?
GIVEN `what kind of corporation the parent is`                        IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc Is the parent a stock corporation, or one of the three kinds of nonstock corporation?
      `the parent is the surviving corporation of the merger`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the parent the corporation that survives the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(e) Are references to the parent's directors and board read as its governing body` IF
    `s 253(e) references to the parent corporation's directors and board are read as references to the members of its governing body and to its governing body` `what kind of corporation the parent is` `the parent is the surviving corporation of the merger`

@export Does section 253 authorize the merger of a corporation with a charitable nonstock corporation whose charitable status would be lost or impaired (s 253(f))?
GIVEN `what kind of corporation the other corporation is`              IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc Is the other corporation a stock corporation, or one of the kinds of nonstock corporation (including a charitable nonstock corporation)?
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired by the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the charitable status of the charitable nonstock corporation be lost or impaired by the merger?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 253(f) Does section 253 authorize the merger with the charitable nonstock corporation` IS
    `s 253(f) this section authorizes the merger with the corporation` `what kind of corporation the other corporation is` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired by the merger`

-- SITUATION: only if your corporation is merging or consolidating with a joint-stock association or a similar unincorporated body.
§§ `s 254: merging or consolidating with a joint-stock or other association`

-- s 254(a). "joint-stock association", as used in the section: an association commonly known as a joint-stock association or company,
-- and any unincorporated association, trust or enterprise having members or outstanding shares or other evidences of financial or
-- beneficial interest -- but not a corporation, partnership or limited liability company.
@export Is the body our corporation is merging with a "joint-stock association" for the purposes of section 254 (s 254(a))?
GIVEN `it is a corporation, partnership or limited liability company`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a corporation, a partnership (general or limited, including a limited liability partnership) or a limited liability company?
      `it is of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or joint-stock company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an association of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or joint-stock company?
      `it has members, or outstanding shares or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have members, or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(a) Is the body a joint-stock association for the purposes of section 254` IF
    `s 254(a) the kind of entity is a joint-stock association` `the kind of body` `it has members, or outstanding shares or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder kinds: an excluded kind stands for "a corporation, partnership or limited liability company"; the trust-like
        -- kinds are all read alike, by whether the body has members or interests.
        `the kind of body` MEANS
            IF `it is a corporation, partnership or limited liability company`
            THEN `a limited liability company`
            ELSE (IF `it is of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or joint-stock company`
                  THEN `a joint-stock association`
                  ELSE `any other unincorporated business or association`)

@export Am I a "stockholder" for the purposes of section 254, as a member or holder of an interest in the association (s 254(a))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder of a corporation in the ordinary sense`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a holder of stock of a corporation?
      `I am a member of the joint-stock association`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the joint-stock association?
      `I hold a share or other evidence of financial or beneficial interest in the joint-stock association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a share of stock, or other evidence of financial or beneficial interest, in the joint-stock association?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(a) Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 254` IF
    `s 254(a) the person is a stockholder for the purposes of s 254` `I am a stockholder of a corporation in the ordinary sense` `I am a member of the joint-stock association` `I hold a share or other evidence of financial or beneficial interest in the joint-stock association`

-- s 254(b). The survivor may be a corporation of this State (stock or nonstock) or a joint-stock association.
@export May the entity our corporation is merging with be the surviving or resulting entity (s 254(b))?
GIVEN `it is a corporation`                                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a corporation?
      `it is a joint-stock association`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a joint-stock association?
      `it was formed under the laws of this State`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it formed under the laws of this State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(b) May the entity be the surviving or resulting entity` IF
    `s 254(b) the entity may be the surviving or resulting entity` `the entity`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: a corporation's kind is not read; a body that is neither a corporation nor a joint-stock association is an LLC.
        `the entity` MEANS Entity WITH
            `kind of entity` IS (IF `it is a corporation` THEN `a corporation` (`a stock corporation`) ELSE (IF `it is a joint-stock association` THEN `a joint-stock association` ELSE `a limited liability company`))
            `where formed` IS (IF `it was formed under the laws of this State` THEN `this State` ELSE `another jurisdiction of the United States`)

@export May our corporation merge into, or consolidate with, a joint-stock association (s 254(b))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                       IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one entity survive and absorb the others (a merger), or do they all form a new entity (a consolidation)?
      `how many of the combining corporations are corporations of this State` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations that are combining are corporations of this State?
      `how many of the combining entities are joint-stock associations`  IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the entities that are combining are joint-stock associations?
      `the law of an association's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of the jurisdiction under which a joint-stock association is formed or organized prohibit the merger or consolidation?
      `the survivor or the new entity may be the surviving or resulting entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting entity a corporation of this State or a joint-stock association? (The question about the entity works this out.)
      `the survivor is one of the combining entities`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger, is the surviving entity one of the entities that are merging? (Answer yes for a consolidation.)
      `the agreement complies with section 254`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state what section 254(c) requires? (The question about the agreement works this out.)
      `the agreement is approved in accordance with section 254`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each constituent entity adopted and approved the agreement as section 254(d) requires? (The question about approval works this out.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(b) May our corporation merge or consolidate with a joint-stock association` IF
    `s 254(b) a corporation of this State may merge or consolidate with a joint-stock association`
        `how the corporations combine`
        `how many of the combining corporations are corporations of this State`
        `how many of the combining entities are joint-stock associations`
        `the law of an association's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation`
        `the survivor or the new entity may be the surviving or resulting entity`
        `the survivor is one of the combining entities`
        `the agreement complies with section 254`
        `the agreement is approved in accordance with section 254`

-- s 254(c). What the agreement with a joint-stock association must state.
@export Does our agreement of merger with a joint-stock association state everything section 254(c) requires (s 254(c))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                       IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one entity survive (a merger), or is a new entity formed (a consolidation)?
      `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting entity a corporation of this State?
      `each corporation and association entered into a written agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did each corporation and joint-stock association enter into a written agreement?
      `the agreement states the terms and conditions`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `the agreement states the mode of carrying it into effect`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect?
      `the agreement states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger whose surviving entity is a corporation of this State: does the agreement state the amendments or changes to its certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the agreement says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a consolidation whose resulting entity is a corporation of this State: does the agreement say its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment? (Answer yes if not.)
      `some shares or interests are to be converted or cancelled`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some shares of a stock corporation, membership interests of a nonstock corporation, or shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests in an association to be converted or cancelled?
      `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling them`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the manner of converting or cancelling them?
      `some shares or interests are not to remain outstanding`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some of those shares or interests not to remain outstanding?
      `their holders are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are their holders to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity?
      `the agreement states what those holders are to receive`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state what those holders are to receive?
      `the agreement provides for cash in lieu of fractions`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests?
      `that provision is consistent with section 155`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it does: is that provision consistent with section 155? (Answer yes if there is no such provision.)
      `the agreement states the other provisions the law of the association requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement set forth the other provisions or facts required in an agreement of merger or consolidation, or required to establish and maintain the joint-stock association by the laws under which it is formed or organized? (Answer yes if nothing more is required.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(c) Does our agreement with a joint-stock association comply with the subsection` IF
    `s 254(c) the agreement complies with the subsection` `how the corporations combine` `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State` `my agreement`
    WHERE
        `my agreement` MEANS `s 254(c) Agreement of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `each such corporation and joint-stock association entered into a written agreement` IS `each corporation and association entered into a written agreement`
            `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS `the agreement states the terms and conditions`
            `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS `the agreement states the mode of carrying it into effect`
            `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS `the agreement states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment` IS `the agreement says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment`
            `some shares, membership interests or financial or beneficial interests are to be converted or cancelled` IS `some shares or interests are to be converted or cancelled`
            `states the manner of converting or cancelling them` IS `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling them`
            `some shares, membership interests or financial or beneficial interests are not to remain outstanding` IS `some shares or interests are not to remain outstanding`
            `the holders of those are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS `their holders are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity`
            `states the cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity that the holders are to receive` IS `the agreement states what those holders are to receive`
            `contains a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests` IS `the agreement provides for cash in lieu of fractions`
            `that provision is consistent with s 155` IS `that provision is consistent with section 155`
            `states the other provisions or facts required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation, or required to establish and maintain a joint-stock association by the laws under which it is formed or organized` IS `the agreement states the other provisions the law of the association requires`

@export May a term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depend on facts outside the agreement (s 254(c))?
GIVEN `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those outside facts operate upon the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(c) May a term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` IF
    `s 254(c) a term of the agreement may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term`

@export Is an event, or a determination or action by a person or body, a fact that a term of our agreement with a joint-stock association may depend on (s 254(c))?
GIVEN `what the term depends on` IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on` @desc Does the term depend on an event, on a determination or action by any person or body (including the corporation), or on something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(c) Is what the term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` IS
    `s 254(c) the item is a fact within the meaning of the closing paragraph` `what the term depends on`

-- s 254(d). Each constituent entity adopts the agreement in its own way: a stock corporation as in section 251, a nonstock corporation
-- as in section 255 (taken as a yes/no), an association under the law of its jurisdiction.
@export Has our constituent entity adopted and approved the agreement with a joint-stock association as section 254(d) requires (s 254(d))?
GIVEN `which kind of constituent entity ours is`                         IS A `s 254(d) Kind of constituent entity` @desc Is your constituent entity a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation, or a joint-stock association?
      `our board adopted the resolution section 251(b) requires`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a stock corporation: has your board adopted a resolution approving the agreement and declaring its advisability?
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement`               IS A NUMBER @desc If a stock corporation: how many votes were cast in favor of the agreement? (Enter 0 if there was no vote.)
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`    IS A NUMBER @desc If a stock corporation: how many votes does all the outstanding stock entitled to vote on the agreement carry?
      `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a stock corporation: is a stockholder vote unnecessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)?
      `our nonstock corporation approved the agreement as section 255 provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a nonstock corporation: did it adopt and approve the agreement in the same manner as section 255 provides?
      `our association adopted the agreement under the law of its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a joint-stock association: was the agreement adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(d) Has our constituent entity adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` IS
    `s 254(d) the constituent entity has adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires`
        `which kind of constituent entity ours is`
        (`s 251(a) the constituent corporation has approved the agreement in accordance with s 251`
            `our board adopted the resolution section 251(b) requires`
            (`s 251(c) the stockholders adopted the agreement` `a stock corporation` `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`)
            `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under section 251(f), (g) or (h)`)
        (JUST `our nonstock corporation approved the agreement as section 255 provides`)
        `our association adopted the agreement under the law of its jurisdiction`

@export When does the agreement with a joint-stock association become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State (s 254(d))?
GIVEN `the date on which a merger of corporations of this State would become effective under section 251` IS A DATE @desc On what date would a merger or consolidation of corporations of this State become effective under section 251, in accordance with section 103? (a date, such as 2028-01-31)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 254(d) When does the agreement become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` IS
    `s 254(d) the date on which the agreement becomes effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` `the date on which a merger of corporations of this State would become effective under section 251`

@export Does our certificate of merger with a joint-stock association state everything section 254(d) requires (s 254(d))?
GIVEN `how the corporations combine`                                 IS A `s 251 Kind of combination` @desc Does one entity survive (a merger), or is a new entity formed (a consolidation)?
      `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting entity a corporation of this State?
      `the surviving or resulting entity is an association formed elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting entity a joint-stock association formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State?
      `the certificate names each constituent entity, its jurisdiction and its type` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name, jurisdiction of formation or organization and type of entity of each constituent entity?
      `the certificate states that the agreement was approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the agreement has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each constituent entity in accordance with section 254(d)?
      `the certificate names the surviving or resulting corporation or association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name of the surviving or resulting corporation or joint-stock association?
      `the certificate states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger whose surviving entity is a corporation of this State: does the certificate state the changes to its certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the certificate says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a consolidation whose resulting entity is a corporation of this State: does the certificate state that its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the certificate says the executed agreement is on file, with the address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation or association, and give the address?
      `the certificate says a copy will be furnished on request without cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that a copy of the agreement will be furnished on request, without cost, to any stockholder or member of any constituent entity?
      `the certificate states the agreement required by section 252(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the surviving or resulting entity is a joint-stock association formed elsewhere: does the certificate state the agreement section 252(d) requires (to be served with process in this State)? (Answer yes if not.)
      `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate executed in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(d) Does our certificate of merger with a joint-stock association state what the subsection requires` IF
    `s 254(d) the certificate of merger or consolidation states what the subsection requires` `how the corporations combine` `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State` `the surviving or resulting entity is an association formed elsewhere` `my certificate`
    WHERE
        `my certificate` MEANS `s 254(d) Certificate of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `states the name, jurisdiction of formation or organization and type of entity of each of the constituent entities` IS `the certificate names each constituent entity, its jurisdiction and its type`
            `states that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent entities in accordance with s 254(d)` IS `the certificate states that the agreement was approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of them`
            `states the name of the surviving or resulting corporation or joint-stock association` IS `the certificate names the surviving or resulting corporation or association`
            `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS `the certificate states the changes in the survivor's certificate of incorporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment to the certificate` IS `the certificate says the resulting corporation's certificate is in an attachment`
            `states that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation or joint-stock association, with the address` IS `the certificate says the executed agreement is on file, with the address`
            `states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished on request and without cost to any stockholder or member of any constituent entity` IS `the certificate says a copy will be furnished on request without cost`
            `states the agreement, if any, required by s 252(d)` IS `the certificate states the agreement required by section 252(d)`
            `executed in accordance with s 103` IS `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103`

@export Can I, as a stockholder or member, get a copy of the agreement with a joint-stock association on request without cost (s 254(d)(7))?
GIVEN `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in lieu of filing the agreement itself?
      `I am a stockholder or member of a constituent entity`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder or member of any of the entities that merged or consolidated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(d)(7) Can I as a stockholder or member get a copy of the agreement without cost` IF
    `s 254(d)(7) the stockholder or member may request a copy of the agreement without cost` `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of the agreement` `I am a stockholder or member of a constituent entity`

-- s 254(e). Which other sections apply "insofar as they are applicable", and what happens to a joint-stock association stockholder's
-- personal liability.
@export Does a given section apply to a merger of our corporation with a joint-stock association (s 254(e))?
GIVEN `which section`                                                    IS A `s 254(e) Section that applies` @desc Which section: 251(d), 251(e), 251(f), 252(d), 259 through 262, or 328?
      `the surviving entity is a corporation of this State`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving entity a corporation of this State?
      `the section is applicable by its own terms`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc For 251(f), 252(d), 259 through 262 and 328: is the section applicable to this merger by its own terms?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(e) Does the section apply to our merger with a joint-stock association` IF
    `s 254(e) the section applies to the merger or consolidation of a corporation and a joint-stock association` `which section` `the surviving entity is a corporation of this State` `the section is applicable by its own terms`

@export In the sections that section 254(e) applies, does "corporation" include a joint-stock association (s 254(e))?
GIVEN `the word corporation is used in an applied section and the reading is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the word "corporation" used in one of the sections section 254(e) applies, in a place where reading it to include a joint-stock association is applicable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(e) Does the word corporation include a joint-stock association in the applied sections` IF
    `s 254(e) the word corporation in the applied section is deemed to include a joint-stock association` `the word corporation is used in an applied section and the reading is applicable`

@export Is my personal liability as a stockholder of the joint-stock association extinguished by the merger (s 254(e))?
GIVEN `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting entity a corporation?
      `I had personal liability as a stockholder of the association when the merger took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have personal liability, as a stockholder of the joint-stock association, at the time of the merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(e) Is my personal liability as a stockholder of the association extinguished by the merger` IS
    `s 254(e) the stockholder's personal liability is extinguished by the merger or consolidation` `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation` `I had personal liability as a stockholder of the association when the merger took place`

@export Can my personal liability as a stockholder of the association become the liability of a later transferee or of another stockholder of the survivor (s 254(e))?
GIVEN `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting entity a corporation?
      `I had personal liability as a stockholder of the association when the merger took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have personal liability, as a stockholder of the joint-stock association, at the time of the merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(e) Can my personal liability pass to a transferee or another stockholder of the survivor` IS
    `s 254(e) the stockholder's personal liability becomes the liability of a subsequent transferee or of another stockholder of the surviving or resulting corporation` `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation` `I had personal liability as a stockholder of the association when the merger took place`

-- s 254(f). Charitable status.
@export Does section 254 authorize merging a charitable nonstock corporation or association into a stock corporation or association if its charitable status would be lost or impaired (s 254(f))?
GIVEN `the merging entity is a charitable nonstock corporation or a charitable joint-stock association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity being merged a charitable nonstock corporation or a charitable joint-stock association?
      `it is to be merged into a stock corporation or a joint-stock association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to be merged into a stock corporation or a joint-stock association?
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired by the merger`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would its charitable status be lost or impaired by the merger?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(f) Does section 254 authorize the merger of the charitable entity` IS
    `s 254(f) this section authorizes the merger of the charitable entity` `the merging entity is a charitable nonstock corporation or a charitable joint-stock association` `it is to be merged into a stock corporation or a joint-stock association` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired by the merger`

@export May a stock corporation or a joint-stock association be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation or charitable association that continues as the survivor (s 254(f))?
GIVEN `the merging entity is a stock corporation or a joint-stock association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity being merged a stock corporation or a joint-stock association?
      `it is merged into a charitable entity that continues as the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it merged into a charitable nonstock corporation or charitable joint-stock association that continues as the surviving corporation or association?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 254(f) May a stock corporation or association be merged into the charitable entity` IS
    `s 254(f) a stock corporation or a joint-stock association may be merged into the charitable entity` `the merging entity is a stock corporation or a joint-stock association` `it is merged into a charitable entity that continues as the survivor`
